The insets control target can make an insets source window (e.g., IME)
in a persistent state of nearly transparent (alpha=0.0001), and trick
the user to click on the certain area of it. If the area has the auto-
fill hints, clicking on it will leak the info to the app, which can be
a security issue.

This CL returns USE_OPACITY from getTouchOcclusionMode if the window
provides insets and is being animated by the control target. So when
the insets source window is nearly transparent, the user cannot click
on it.

#b/493560718

